en.use:
Use to assess the clinical or pathological stage group for endometrial cancer. 

The guideline maps the individual tumor extent findings to the overall prognostic stage:

stage I: tumor confined to the corpus uteri;

stage IA: No invasion or invasion &lt; half the thickness of the myometrium;

stage IB: Invasion ≥ half the thickness of the myometrium;

stage II: Invasion into the cervical stroma but not outside the uterus;

stage III:Local and/or regional spread;

stage IIIA: Invasion of uterine serosa and/or adnexa;

stage IIIB: Vaginal growth and/or parametrial growth;

stage IIIC: Metastases to pelvic nodes and/or paraaortic lymph nodes;

stage IIIC1: Positive pelvic nodes;

stage IIIC2: Positive paraaortic glands regardless of positive or negative pelvic glands;

stage IV: Spread to bladder and/or rectum and/or distant metastases;

stage IVA: Spread to the bladder and/or rectum;

stage IVB: Distant metastases, including intra-abdominal metastases and/or inguinal metastases.
